<<<
+ toy, of which no-one can be said to know, though different people make different guesses at, the original meaning. The OED?’s description of it, as it now survives, is: ‘In | modern literary use (after some of the examples in Shakspere), an expression of indignant scorn ap- | pended to a quoted expression or to a statement of fact’.
===
+ toy, of which no-one can be said to know, though different people make different guesses at, the original meaning. The OED's description of it, as it now survives, is: 'In modern literary use (after some of the examples in Shakspere), an expression of indignant scorn appended to a quoted expression or to a statement of fact'.
>>>

